<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iranun</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Illanun, Ilanun, Iranun people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iranun are a people of the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a> around Illana Bay in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, with communities also in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a>. In the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries Iranun fleets, allied with the Sulu Sultanate, were renowned as maritime raiders, attacking coasts from the Philippines to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> and taking captives for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iranun.jpg" alt="Iranun" width="320" height="528" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: filhistory.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Iranun_(Ilanun)_Moro_%27pirate%27.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
